{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Whatever touches its flesh.</b> Any food item that touches and absorbs from it." "<b>Shall become holy.</b> To become like it — if it is disqualified, it is disqualified; and if it is valid, it is eaten in accordance with its degree of holiness." "<b>And whatever its blood splashes onto the garment.</b> And if its blood was splashed onto the garment — that place of blood on the garment upon which it splashes — you shall wash inside the courtyard." "<b>That splashes.</b> It shall splash — as in ״וְלֹא יִטֶּה לָאָרֶץ מִנְלָם״ (Job 15) — it shall bend."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:16.008324752Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}